{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795286979,"nonce":"vc6gydR7cyihI/cPXePJjW1E4zE=","title":"The terrain has features, and planes and shots collide with them","message":"\u003e We need to add flares to defend against missiles. We should also pull in game assets from separate branches and keep reading git bug. We also want full screen, \"fuller\" HUD, etc. We have various plane models (players model up planes as they rack up kills) on another branch, but they are not currently destructible. If feasible, deconstruct models into pieces that fit the current model. Current model: destroyed wings or fuselage should be a very quick crash. Add assets (audio, terrain, planes, etc.) as they arrive on different branches. Terrain features need collision detection too.\n\n**Today.** The ground is flat. The blocks on it are decoration, and nothing can hit them.\n\n**Outcome.** The rules hold the terrain: the height of the ground at each place, and the features that stand on it. A plane that touches the ground or a feature is destroyed, and a bullet or a missile ends there. Bots stay clear of both. The client draws the terrain from the same data. A terrain asset from another branch can replace the generated one, if it gives its heights.\n\n**Done when.** Tests of the rules show a crash into a hill and into a feature, a shot that a hill stops, and bots that fly a match over the terrain without a crash.\n\nBelongs to the plan, issue 1d9449d.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}